      "content": "Most major social media platforms, including Meta, X (former Twitter), and TikTok, explicitly exclude political satire from hate speech policies as long as it does not target protected groups with demonstrable harm. The industry standard generally focuses on context and intent, flagging content only if it criminalizes individuals based on their membership in a protected group or incites violence, rather than just making a political point through humor or exaggeration. While there is no single universal \"line,\" the consensus is that political speech must have clear evidence of being hate speech—such as promoting violence or advocacy to encroach on another person's territory—to be prohibited rather than defamed.",
