      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no true industry consensus on this issue; instead, major platforms like X and Meta operate under vastly different legal frameworks and strategic risk tolerances that dictate their specific interpretations. X's recent policy shift largely aligns with the \"pragmatic\" side used for free speech advocacy, prioritizing market growth over legal liability in many regions, while Meta and Google often prioritize legal compliance and user safety in courts that strictly interpret hate speech. Consequently, the \"consensus\" you heard is often more of a reactive patchwork of legal necessities and corporate strategy rather than a unified ethical standard.",
